###  http://voparis-ns.obspm.fr/rdf/ihdea/refframe/MeanEclipticJ2000
:MeanEclipticJ2000 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:label "Body-related Mean Ecliptic, dynamical equinox of J2000" .


###  http://voparis-ns.obspm.fr/rdf/ihdea/refframe/MeanEquatorEquinoxDate
:MeanEquatorEquinoxDate rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:comment """The Body Mean Ecliptic and Equinox of Date frame is defined as follows:
- +Z axis is aligned with the north-pointing vector normal to the mean orbital plane of the Body;
- +X axis points along the ''mean equinox'', which is defined as the intersection of the Body's mean orbital plane with the body's mean equatorial plane. It is aligned with the cross product of the north-pointing vectors normal to the Body's mean equator and mean orbit plane of date;
- +Y axis is the cross product of the Z and X axes and completes the right-handed frame;
-  the origin of this frame is the body's center of mass.
  
The mathematical model used to obtain the orientation of the Body's mean equator and equinox of date frame is the 1976 IAU precession model, built into SPICE.
  
The mathematical model used to obtain the mean orbital plane of the Body is the 1980 IAU obliquity model, also built into SPICE.
  
The base frame for the 1976 IAU precession model is J2000.
    \"""" ;
                        rdfs:label "Body-related Mean Equator and Equinox of Date" .


###  http://voparis-ns.obspm.fr/rdf/ihdea/refframe/MeanEquatorJ2000
:MeanEquatorJ2000 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "Body-related Mean Equator, dynamical equinox of J2000" .


