             rdfs:comment """Lutetia solar orbital frame is defined as a two-vector style dynamic frames as follows:
 -  The position of the sun relative to the comet is the primary vector: the X axis points from the
    asteroid to the Sun.
 -  The inertially referenced velocity of the sun relative to the asteroid is the secondary vector: the Y
    axis is the component of this velocity vector orthogonal to the X axis.
 -  The Z axis is X cross Y, completing the right-handed reference frame.""" ;
             rdfs:label "Solar orbital centered on asteroid LUTETIA" .


